================================================================================
MILESTONE 58 — EXECUTION CHANGES
Success Response Logging, Raw AI Text Viewer & Overwrite Confirmation
Branch: feature/m58-success-logging-diagnosis-confirmation
================================================================================

SUMMARY
-------
Implemented success forensic logging for the clinical AI diagnosis flow, a
"Respuestas exitosas" viewer in the Profile Pruebas accordion, exact binding to
the backend diagnosticReport/mealSuggestions payload, and an overwrite
confirmation dialog. Delivered under a strict TDD loop with one logical commit
per step.

VERIFICATION
------------
- fvm flutter analyze  -> No issues found! (197.5s)
- fvm flutter test     -> 875 passed, 0 failed
- SDK: fvm (Flutter 3.29.0, Dart 3.7.0)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TASK 1 — Success forensic logging (SQLite)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rationale: error forensics already existed (m51–m55), but successful responses
(including the raw JSON/text, request URL and timestamp) were discarded after
parsing. Auditing the AI diagnosis workflow requires the exact payload that
succeeded.

Created:
- lib/core/models/success_log_entry.dart
    SuccessLogEntry {id, timestamp, statusCode, label, requestUrl, requestBody,
    responseBody} with toMap()/fromMap(). UTC ISO-8601 timestamps.
- lib/core/data/success_log_repository.dart
    SuccessLogRepository {Future<void> record(...); Future<List<...>> getAll();}.
- lib/core/data/local_success_log_repository.dart
    SQLite implementation delegating to DatabaseHelper.
- lib/core/mocks/mock_success_log_repository.dart
    In-memory reverse-ordered store for mock flavors and widget tests.
- test/data/success_log_repository_test.dart
    Persistence/newest-first ordering and the v19 -> v20 migration (preserves
    existing local_error_logs rows).

Modified:
- lib/core/database/database_schema.dart
    version 19 -> 20; createLocalSuccessLogTable() with a
    (timestamp DESC, id DESC) index; createAll() and upgrade() call it.
- lib/core/database/database_helper.dart
    insertSuccessLog() / getSuccessLogs().
- lib/core/data/ai_diagnosis_repository.dart
    Optional SuccessLogRepository + clock injection; _recordSuccess() persists
    the raw exchange after a report is parsed and saved. Failure-safe (a storage
    error never discards the report). Label = 'clinical_diagnosis'.
- test/data/ai_diagnosis_repository_test.dart
    Success captured on 200 (URL, request body, response body, status, label,
    timestamp) and no success entry on failure.

Commit: feat(m58): persist successful AI diagnosis responses in local forensics log

